  "live_records": {
    "q-146309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146309",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the covariance between $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times [0,4].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $h(y)=\\frac{y}{8}.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
